\name{cellucid_history_journal_undo}
\alias{cellucid_history_journal_undo}
\title{Restore from Recently deleted}
\usage{
cellucid_history_journal_undo(viewer, entry, tracker)
}
\arguments{
\item{viewer}{A viewer \code{\link{cellucid_view}()} or \code{\link{cellucid_serve}()} returned.}
\item{entry}{An entry of Recently deleted, by its id (history_summary counts them). Text. Required.}
\item{tracker}{A tracker by its name or its id (history_summary lists them); the tracker in use when left out. Text (at least 1 character). Left out unless given (the viewer then chooses as its own control does).}
}
\value{
A \code{cellucid_action_request}, at once and invisibly: the action is sent now, or when the viewer's channel opens.
\code{\link{cellucid_action_result}(request)} returns its outcome: a list of \code{branch} (The first branch a restore as new made of the steps it applied again), \code{entry}, \code{journal} (The entry the restore itself made (undoable)), \code{report} (The steps a restore as new applied again and what became of each (empty for an exact restore)), \code{restored}.
}
\description{
Undo an edit of the history (a delete, a rename, a note, \ldots) from Recently deleted: exactly as it was when nothing changed it since, else as new objects ("X (restored)", removed steps applied again as a branch). Undoing a rename whose old name was taken since is refused, naming the name to use instead.
}
\details{
The viewer's action \code{history.journal.undo} (History). It moves the viewer's history, as the person's Undo, Redo or a click on a step does: it makes no step of the history.
}
\seealso{
\code{\link{cellucid_act}()} sends any action by its type, and \code{\link{cellucid_action_result}()}
collects its answer.
}
\examples{
if (interactive() && requireNamespace("SeuratObject", quietly = TRUE)) {
  data("pbmc_small", package = "SeuratObject")
  viewer <- cellucid_view(SeuratObject::UpdateSeuratObject(pbmc_small))
  request <- cellucid_history_journal_undo(viewer, entry = "j0")
  print(request)
  # cellucid_action_result(request) waits for its outcome.
  cellucid_stop(viewer)
}
}
